values  (171, 2436, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms persist.'),
        (172, 2436, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.'),
        (173, 2655, 'Mises en garde', 'This product is for adult use only.  Take with food. Avoid two hours prior to or until hours after taking other medications.  Do not use if you have a copper storage or metabolism disorder, sush as Wilson''s Disease.  Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you have impaired liver function, or if you are taking levodopa or tetracyclines.  Discontinue use if you experience a prolonges flushing, burning, tingling or itching sensation on the face, arms or chest.'),
        (174, 2655, 'Contre-indications', 'No reports known'),
        (175, 2655, 'Mises en garde', 'No reports known.'),
        (176, 2789, 'Mises en garde', 'Do not exceed the recommended dosage.  Keep away from eyes, mucous membranes, wounds, damaged or irritated skin.  If rash or excessive irritation occurs, discontinue use.  Do not bandage or use heating pad.  If condition worsens, or if symptoms persist for more than 7 days, or clear up and occur again within a few days, discontinue use of this product and consult a physician.  FOR EXTERNAL USE ONLY. Do not use for children under 2 years old except on the advise of a physician.'),
        (177, 2789, 'Contre-indications', 'If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, consult a physician before using this product.  Do not use if you are allergic to salicylates or if you are taking anticoagulant medications.'),
        (178, 2789, 'Réactions indésirables', 'None known.'),
        (179, 2359, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you have rheumatoid arthritis.  Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you have a progressive systemic disease, such as tuberculosis, leukosis, collagenosis, multiple sclerosis, AIDS, HIV infection. Consult a health care practitioner prior to using if you have auto-immune disorders.  Consult a health care practitioner prior to using if you are taking ummunosuppressants.  Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms persist.'),
        (180, 2359, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.
Do not use if you ahve an allergy to Asteraceae/compositae (daisy) family.'),
        (181, 2738, 'Contre-indications', 'S.O.'),
        (182, 2392, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner prior use if you have rheumatoid arthritis.  Consult a health care practitioner prior use if you have a progressive systemic disease such as tuberculosis, leucosis, collagenosis, multiple sclerosis, AIDS, HIV infection.  Consult a health care practitioner prior use if you have autoimmune disorders.  Consult a health care practitioner prior using if you are taking immunosuppressants.  Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms persist.'),
        (183, 2392, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.  Do not use if you have allergy to Asteraceae/Compositae (daisy) family.'),
        (184, 2695, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms persist or worsen.'),
        (185, 2485, 'Mises en garde', 'Not intended for use as a substitute for sleep. Consult a doctor prior to use if you have high blood pressure, glaucoma, or overactive bladder, or are taking lithium. Consumption with other caffeine-containing products (e.g. medications, coffee, tea, colas, cocoa, guarana, maté), or products that may increase blood pressure (e.g. bitter orange extract, synephrine, octopamine, ephedra, ephedrine) is not recommended. Consult your doctor if you intend to take more than a single tablet  per day, and are of childbearing age, pregnant or breastfeeding. NOT TO BE GIVEN TO CHILDREN.'),
        (186, 2485, 'Réactions indésirables', 'At doses greater than 600 mg per day, caffeine may cause anxiety, rapid heart rate, palpitations, insomnia, restlessness, nervousness, tremor and headache. In the event of an allergic reaction, discontinue use.'),
        (187, 2453, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you have impaired liver function.  Consult a health care practitioner if diarrhoea persists.'),
        (188, 2453, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if pregnant or breastfeeding.  Keep out of reach of children.'),
        (189, 2379, 'Mises en garde', 'Discontinue if hypersensitivity occurs such as edematous dermatitis and eczema. Do not take internally.'),
        (190, 2379, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if allergic to Asteraceae/Compositae (daisy family).
Do not use if you are pregnant or brestfeeding.  Do  not use on open wounds or broken skin.'),
        (191, 2675, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if pregnant or breastfeeding.
