        (192, 2512, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms persist or worsen.'),
        (193, 2706, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if pregnant or breastfeeding.'),
        (194, 2737, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if you have a copper storage or metabolism disorder, such as Wilson''s disease.'),
        (195, 2504, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms persist or worsen.  Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you have a liver disease.'),
        (196, 2504, 'Réactions indésirables', 'Hypersensitivity/allergy is known to occur, in which case, discontinue use.'),
        (197, 2414, 'Mises en garde', 'For external use only.  If rash or irritation occurs discontinue use.  The application of external heat, such as an electric heating pad, may result in excessive skin irritation or skin burn.  Avoid contact with eyes and mucous membranes.  Do not bandage.  Do not apply to wounds or damaged skin.
If you experience pain, swelling or blistering, stop use and get medical help right away.'),
        (198, 2658, 'Mises en garde', 'Avoid using two (2) hours prior to or until four (4) hours after taking other medications.'),
        (199, 2353, 'Mises en garde', 'Consulter un fournisseur de soins de santé si vous avez une obstruction de la vésicule biliaire ou du canal biliaire, une hernie hiatale ou avez un reflux gastro-oesophagien. Ne pas utiliser plus de 2 semaines.'),
        (200, 2353, 'Contre-indications', 'Ne pas utiliser en cas de grossesse ou d''allaitement.'),
        (201, 2737, 'Mises en garde', 'N/A'),
        (202, 2737, 'Réactions indésirables', 'N/A'),
        (203, 2550, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner for prolonged use. Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms persist or worsen. Consult a health care practitioner before use if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.'),
        (204, 2558, 'Mises en garde', 'Do not use if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.'),
        (205, 2558, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if you are taking wafarin.'),
        (206, 2383, 'Mises en garde', 'Do not use if pregnant or breastfeeding. Do not use if you have liver afflictions or are using anticonvulsants. Do not exceed recommended dosage. May cause constipation.'),
        (207, 2764, 'Mises en garde', 'Doctor''s supervision is necessary before administering to babies (0-12 months).  Protect from direct sunlight.  Arnica hypersensitivity.  In individual cases, hypersensitivity reactions are possible in persons hypersensitive to composites (Arnica).  If symptoms persist or worsen, consult a health care practitioner.'),
        (814, 2500, 'Réactions indésirables', 'S.O.'),
        (208, 2640, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a healthcare practitioner prior to use if you are taking tetracyclines, hormone replacement therapy, or blood thinners. Consult a healthcare practitioner if you experience gastrointestinal discomfort, or if symptoms persist after 6 months. Use only as directed. Keep out of the reach of children. Not for use by persons under the age of 18. Take a few hours before or a few hours after taking other medications.'),
        (209, 2640, 'Réactions indésirables', 'None if taken and stored as directed.'),
        (210, 2673, 'Mises en garde', 'S.O.'),
        (211, 2469, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms persist or worsen.
Do not use if safety seal is broken.'),
        (212, 2482, 'Mises en garde', 'Arrêter l''usage en présence de diarrhée. Doit être utilisé avec précaution pendant la grossesse et les menstruations.'),
        (213, 2482, 'Contre-indications', 'Ne doit pas être utilisé si l''on souffre de maladies rénales. Ne pas administrer aux enfants souffrant de parasites intestinaux.'),
        (214, 2482, 'Réactions indésirables', 'Au dosage recommandé, peut avoir une légère action laxative ou une irritation intestinale.'),
        (215, 2445, 'Mises en garde', 'Consultez un praticien de la santé si les symptômes persistent ou s''aggravent.  Consultez un praticien de la santé avant l''usage si vous êtes enceinte ou si vous allaitez.'),
        (216, 2696, 'Mises en garde', 'Discontinue use if skin irritation develops or increases.  If irritation persists, consult a health care practitioner.  Avoid contact with eyes.  If contact occurs, rinse thoroughly with water.  For external use only.  Keep out of reach of children.  Consult a health care practitioner prior to use on children less than six months of age.'),
        (217, 2770, 'Mises en garde', 'Do not drink directly from vial due to the sharp glass edges.  Consult a health care practitioner if you experience blood in the urine, fever, or sustained, unclear or new symptoms.  Consult a health care practitioner before using if pregnant of breastfeeding.  Do not use in children under 12 years of age before a health care practitioner is consulted.  The effect of a homeopathic remedy may be compromised by harmful lifestyles and the use of irritative/pleasurable substances.  If you are taking any other medications, discuss with your health care practitioner.'),
        (218, 2770, 'Contre-indications', 'Hypersensitivity to bee venom.'),
        (219, 2770, 'Réactions indésirables', 'Side effect: Because this remedy contains Hydrargyrum bichloratum (mercury), patients may occasionally experience allergic reactions.  Increased salivation may occur after the use of Pascorenal Forte.  If this occurs, discontinue use.  Homeopathic remedies may transiently worsen existing symptoms (initial aggravation).  If this occurs, stop this medicinal product and consult your health care practitioner.  If you experience any side effects, please make sure to inform your health care practitioner.'),
        (220, 2756, 'Mises en garde', 'Consulter un praticien de la santé si les symptômes persistent ou s''aggravent, ou pour un usage prolongé. Consulter un praticien de la santé avant l''usage si vous êtes enceinte ou si vous allaitez.'),
