        (310, 2335, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not take with blood thinners. Do not take with Vitamin A derivatives called "retinoids" (prescribed to treat acne). Do not take with Vitamin D (for treatment). PHARMATON CAPSULES are contraindicated in patients with disturbances of calcium metabolism (e.g., hypercalaemia and hypercalciuria), with hypervitaminosis, with renal insufficiency, during therapy with retinoids (e.g., against acne) or vitamin D, and in patients with known hypersensitivity to any ingredients of the compound. This product is contraindicated in patients with a history of allergy to soya or peanuts. In case of rare hereditary conditions that may be incompatible with an excipient of the product, the use of the product is contraindicated.'),
