        (576, 2315, 'Réactions indésirables', 'S.O.'),
        (578, 2595, 'Réactions indésirables', 'May cause nausea, vomitting, diarrhea, and/or abdominal cramps. Discontinue use and consult a health care practitioner if these symptoms are severe.
Rare, unpredictable cases of liver injury associated with green tea extract-containing products have been reposted  (in Canada and internationally).'),
        (579, 2595, 'Mises en garde', 'Ensure to drink enough fluid before, during, and after exercise.
If you have a liver disorder, consult a health care practitioner prior to use. Stop use if you develop symptoms of liver trouble such as yellowing of the skin/eyes (jaundice), stomach pain, dark urine, sweating, nausea, unusual tiredness and/or loss of appetite and consult a health care practitioner.
Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you have an iron deficiency or are taking blood thinners.
If you have kidney stones, consult a health care practitioner prior to use.'),
        (580, 2595, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use with other potassium-containing supplements or with potassium-containing salt-substitutes.
Do not use if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.
If you are taking antibiotics, do not use this product.
If you are taking nitroglycerin, do not use this product.'),
        (581, 2774, 'Mises en garde', 'S.O.'),
        (582, 2328, 'Réactions indésirables', 'Une hypersensibilité (p. ex. une allergie) peut se manifester.
Si tel est le cas, cesser l''usage.
Cesser l''usage en cas de problèmes gastro-intestinaux tels que des crampes abdominales, des nausées, des vomissements ou de la diarrhée.'),
        (583, 2765, 'Réactions indésirables', 'Hypersensitivity/allergy can occur; in which case, discontinue use. Diuretic effect may occur.'),
        (584, 2765, 'Contre-indications', 'If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, do not use this product.'),
        (585, 2765, 'Mises en garde', 'If symptoms persist or worsen, or if new symptoms develop, discontinue use and consult a health care practitioner. If you are taking prescription medications, consult a health care practitioner prior to use. If you have indigestion, diarrhea due to Spleen deficiency, or a white, greasy tongue coating, consult a health care practitioner prior to use. If you have a yin deficiency, sunken spleen qi, or cold from deficiency with spermatorrhea, consult a health care practitioner prior to use.'),
        (586, 2328, 'Mises en garde', 'Consulter un praticien de soins de santé avant d''en faire l''usage si vous prenez des anticoagulants.
Consulter un praticien de soins de santé avant l''utilisation si vous avez déjà souffert de calculs rénaux.
Consulter un praticien de soins de santé si les symptômes persistent ou s''aggravent.
Si vous êtes enceinte ou allaitez, consulter un praticien de soins de santé avant l''utilisation.'),
        (587, 2329, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner before use if you are pregnant or breastfeeding. Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms persist or worsen.'),
        (588, 2693, 'Mises en garde', 'If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, do not use this product.
If symptoms persist or worsen, or if new symptoms develop, discontinue use and consult a health care practitioner.
If you are taking prescription medications, consult a health care practitioner prior to use.
If you have serious or major conditions, any type of acute infection or excess, consult a health care prior to use.
Do not use in case of yin-deficiency heat.
If you have hypokalemia, high blood pressure, or a kidney or cardiovascular disorder, do not use this products.
If you are taking thiazide diuretics, cardiac glyocosides , corticosteroids, stimulant laxatives or other mediations which may aggravate electrolyte imbalance, do not use this products.'),
        (589, 2352, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you are sensitive to wheat germ or baker''s yeast.'),
        (590, 2352, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if you are pregnant or breastfeeding or if you are taking immune suppressive medication.'),
        (591, 2682, 'Contre-indications', 'S.O.'),
        (592, 2759, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms persist or worsen.
Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you are breastfeeding.
Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you are taking blood thinners.'),
        (593, 2759, 'Réactions indésirables', 'Hypersensitivity, such as an allergy, has been known to occur; in which case, discontinue use.
Some people may experience sore mouth, mouth ulcers and/or gastrointestinal discomfort.'),
        (594, 2759, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if you are allergic to plants of the Asteraceae/Compositae/Daisy family.
Do not use if you are pregnant.'),
        (595, 2688, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner if symptoms worsen. Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.'),
        (596, 2660, 'Réactions indésirables', 'S.O.'),
        (597, 2660, 'Mises en garde', 'S.O.'),
        (598, 2732, 'Mises en garde', 'S.O.'),
        (599, 2677, 'Mises en garde', 'If accidental ingestion occurs, seek urgent medical attention or contact a Poison Control Centre.  Keep out of reach of children.  If symptoms persist or worsen, consult a health care practitioner.  If you have epilepsy or asthma, consult a health care practitioner prior to use. Do not expose the applied area to the sun for 24 to 48 hours after application. If you have broken, irritated or sensitive skin, do not use this product.'),
        (600, 2677, 'Réactions indésirables', 'If you experience nausea, dizziness, headache or an allergic reaction, discontinue use.'),
        (601, 2677, 'Contre-indications', 'Do not use if pregnant or breastfeeding.'),
        (602, 2484, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you suffer from a hormone-sensitive condition, anxiety, depression, a psychological disorder, high blood pressure, diabetes, a bleeding disorder, or if you have ulcerative colitis, Crohn''s disease or hemorrhoids. Consult a health care practitioner prior to use if you are trying to conceive or if you are taking propranolol. Ensure to drink enough fluid before, during, and after exercise.
If symptoms persist or worsen, or if new symptoms develop, consult a health care practitioner.
If you have hypertension or are taking medication(s) for hypertension, consult a health care practitioner prior to use.
Do not use if you have fire from yin deficiency.
Consult a healthcare practitioner prior to use if you have benign prostate hypertrophy and/or prostate cancer.
Adult women: Consult a healthcare practitioner if you experience abnormal hair growth.'),
        (603, 2754, 'Mises en garde', 'Consult a health care practitioner if you are pregnant or breastfeeding. Some people may experience gastrointestinal disturbances, fever, chills, hot flushing, dizziness, malaise, acne. If you are taking prescription medications, consult a health care practitioner prior to use. Keep out of the reach of children.'),
